{
  "diagnosis": "The attempt failed at compilation due to an inconsistent type for the loop-carried variable 'count' in the stats kernel. It is initialized as a Python int (int32), but inside the loop it is incremented by tl.sum(mask, 0), which returns a uint32. Triton requires loop-carried variables to have a consistent type throughout the loop, hence the compilation assertion error.",
  "outcome": "Compilation failed, so no runtime or correctness validation occurred. The stats kernel cannot execute in its current form and does not produce any output.",
  "next_step": "Repair the stats kernel by initializing 'count' with tl.zeros((), dtype=tl.uint32) or by removing it entirely if it is unused, ensuring all loop-carried variables maintain a consistent Triton type. Review all other loop-carried variables for type consistency. After fixing, re-measure for correctness and performance."
}

